---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/page.css';

// Describes only what the booking system actually does. If it changes, so
// must this page.
const contact = 'aafkedailycalendar@gmail.com';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy | Aafke Beukema"
  description="How the booking page at aafke.co.uk uses your information."
>
  <main>
    <header class="masthead">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="tagline">
        How I use the information you give me when you book a chat through
        this website.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated 5 October 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="collect">
      <h2 id="collect">What I collect</h2>
      <p>When you book a chat at <a href="/talktome">aafke.co.uk/talktome</a>, the form asks for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name</li>
        <li>your email address</li>
        <li>your phone number, if you choose to give it</li>
        <li>what you'd like to chat about, if you choose to say</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="spaced">
        That's the minimum needed to arrange the meeting. The site has no
        accounts, and doesn't use analytics or advertising.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="use">
      <h2 id="use">How I use it</h2>
      <p>
        Only to arrange and manage the meeting you asked for: to send you a
        calendar invitation, set up the Google Meet, and get in touch about the
        meeting if I need to. Your information is never sold, and never used
        for advertising or marketing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="stored">
      <h2 id="stored">Where it's stored</h2>
      <p>
        Bookings are made in my Google Calendar. When you book, the calendar
        event for your chosen time is updated with your details, you're added
        as a guest, and a Google Meet is created for it. Google then emails you
        the invitation.
      </p>
      <p class="spaced">
        Your booking details are stored in Google Calendar, not in a separate
        database on this website. Google handles them as described in
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="cancel">
      <h2 id="cancel">Cancelling</h2>
      <p>
        Your booking includes a cancellation link. It contains a random code,
        and a copy of that code is stored privately on the calendar event, so
        only someone with your link can cancel the booking.
      </p>
      <p class="spaced">
        When you cancel, your name, email address, phone number, message, the
        Google Meet and the cancellation code are all removed from the event,
        and the time becomes available to book again.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="google">
      <h2 id="google">Google Calendar access</h2>
      <p>
        The booking system connects only to my own Google Calendar. It reads it
        to find the times I've marked as available, and edits those events to
        make and cancel bookings. It never accesses your Google account.
      </p>
      <p class="spaced">
        Its use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="technical">
      <h2 id="technical">Visiting the website</h2>
      <p>
        This website is hosted by a web hosting provider and loads its fonts
        from Google Fonts. When you visit, your browser connects to those
        services, which can see technical information such as your IP address.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="questions">
      <h2 id="questions">Questions</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions about your information, including asking to
        see it or have it removed, email
        <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .updated {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  li + li {
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }
</style>
